<title>USA: Wilmington, Del., GOP offers alternate budget.</title>
<headline>Wilmington, Del., GOP offers alternate budget.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Wilmington, Del., Republican Task Force unveiled an alternate city budget criticizing Mayor Jim Sills' spending plan, which comes up for a vote Thursday night.</p>
<p>The GOP budget proposes to save money by eliminating about 30 city jobs, bidding out certain city services and combining a number of county and city functions.</p>
<p>An official from the mayor's office said Sills has not seen the Republicans' proposal.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
